# Dashboard UI

## Purpose

Keep the bundled dashboard consistent, path-agnostic, and reusing its shared primitives so it
works under any adapter and any mount path.

## Why it exists

The dashboard lives in `packages/core/src/ui` (a Vite + React app, own `package.json`, name
`ui`), is built and copied into `@lensjs/core`'s `dist/ui` (`build:ui` + `copy-front-build.cjs`),
and is served by adapters. It must never assume where it is mounted or which API base it talks
to — those are discovered at runtime.

## Stack

- React 19 + `react-router-dom` v7 (route table via `useRoutes`).
- Server state via `@tanstack/react-query`.
- Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` (not PostCSS); icons via `lucide-react`.
- Timestamps via `@lensjs/date` (`humanDifferentDate`, `formatTimeAgo`), never `Date`/dayjs ad hoc.

## Path-agnostic build (do not break)

`vite.config.ts` sets `base: "./"` and the `prod` script sets `VITE_API_URL=''` so all asset and
API URLs are RELATIVE. Config is fetched at runtime: `App.tsx` does
`fetch(prepareApiUrl("/lens-config"))` and puts the result in `ConfigContext` before rendering
routes ([App.tsx](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/App.tsx)). There is no `window.__LENS`/HTML
injection.

Provider order (outer -> inner): `QueryClientProvider` -> `BrowserRouter` -> `ConfigContext`
-> `ThemeProvider` -> `Suspense` -> `Router`.

## Structure & layering (under `src/ui/src`)

`components/` (reusable, presentational), `containers/` (smart: data + routing glue),
`views/` (routed page presentation + `columns`), `router/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`, `types/`,
`interfaces/`. Keep each file in the folder matching its role.

The per-feature QUARTET (requests, queries, cache, exceptions, mail) repeats exactly:
`containers/<f>/<F>Container.tsx` + `<F>DetailsContainer.tsx`, `views/<f>/<F>Table.tsx` +
`columns.tsx` + `<F>Details.tsx`. Containers call the feature hook + `useLoadMore` and
`React.lazy`-import the view; views are pure props-in markup;
[RequestsContainer.tsx](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/containers/requests/RequestsContainer.tsx)
is the reference.

## Data fetching & config-driven URLs

- Build every URL with `prepareApiUrl()`
  ([utils/api.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/utils/api.ts)) over a base path from config.
- Endpoint bases come from the injected config (`config.api.requests|queries|cache|exceptions|
  mail|truncate`) via `useConfig()`
  ([utils/context.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/utils/context.ts)); route strings come from
  `getRoutesPaths(config)` ([router/routes/index.tsx](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/router/routes/index.tsx)).
  NEVER hardcode `/lens` or any API path.
- List pagination: the feature hook exposes a memoized `loadMore*` object
  `{ initialData, meta, loading, fetchRawPage }` consumed by `useLoadMore`
  ([hooks/useLoadMore.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/hooks/useLoadMore.ts)), which returns
  `{ data, hasMore, loading, loadMore }`.
- Detail fetching prefers React Query hooks in
  [useTanstackApi.ts](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/hooks/useTanstackApi.ts). Two data layers
  currently coexist (`useLensApi` + `useState` vs React Query) — this is debt; do not add a
  third, and prefer consolidating onto React Query when you touch a feature.

## Component conventions

- Functional components only; one per file; PascalCase `.tsx` filenames; hooks are `use*.ts`;
  column factories are `columns.tsx` exporting `getColumns()`.
- Type props with an inline type for tiny components or a named `interface` for richer ones;
  the data-driven `Table<T>` is generic ([Table.tsx](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/components/Table.tsx)).
- Reuse shared primitives: `Table`, `DetailPanel`, `TabbedDataViewer`, `JsonViewer`, `Modal`,
  and the badges. Semantic colors live INSIDE the badge components
  ([CacheActionBadge.tsx](mdc:packages/core/src/ui/src/components/CacheActionBadge.tsx),
  `MethodBadge`, `StatusCode`) — never inline color logic at call sites.

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes; dark mode ONLY (`ThemeProvider` forces `dark`, `toggleTheme` is a
  no-op — do not add a light theme). Reuse tokens/utilities from `index.css` (e.g.
  `.card-panel`).
- Compose conditional classes with `tailwind-merge` (`twMerge`), as in `Table.tsx`/`LoadMore.tsx`.
- Declare any new runtime dependency in the UI `package.json` (e.g. `tailwind-merge` is
  currently resolved via hoisting from core — declare deps you import).

## Dev & build

- Dev server: `pnpm run dev:front`. After UI changes, rebuild core (`pnpm build`) so `dist/ui`
  reflects them (adapters serve `dist/ui`, not `src/ui`).

## AI must never

- Hardcode `/lens`, an API path, or an absolute asset URL.
- Read config from a global/`window` instead of `useConfig()`.
- Add feature data-fetching/loading/caching state by hand when a hook/React Query covers it.
- Introduce a light theme or inline badge/status colors at call sites.
